  "title": "Military leader in Judah after the fall of Jerusalem",
  "era": "exile",
  "lifespan": "c. 600s BC",
  "summary": "Johanan, son of Kareah, was one of the military leaders who remained in Judah after Babylon destroyed Jerusalem in 586 BC. He warned Gedaliah against Ishmael's murder plot but was not heard. After Gedaliah was killed, he led the remaining Jews to Egypt, contrary to the prophet Jeremiah's warning.",
